---
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user explicitly requests deleting files, do not use Cursor's built-in Delete tool. Use a bounded Shell command instead.

For files, use:

```sh
rm -f -- <exact-path>
```

For directories, prefer `rmdir` when empty. Use:

```sh
rm -rf -- <exact-path>
```

only when recursive directory deletion was explicitly requested.

Always use explicit paths. Do not introduce wildcards, broaden the requested target, or delete unrelated files. Verify that the requested target no longer exists after deletion.
